WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.166
King James! King James!

00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:27.666
Here to help our house go right!

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:32.125
You’re going to love it here.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.666
Greatest city in the world.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.375
You’re the next chapter in its long history of greatness.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.750
So wonderful to welcome LeBron to the Lakers family.

00:00:53.291 --> 00:00:56.291
We’re definitely going to the tournament this year.

00:00:56.291 --> 00:00:57.625
We’d better.

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:09.291
Go back to Cleveland! We don’t want you here!

00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:09.875
Seize him!

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:10.875
Long live the Black Mamba!

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:13.000
The real GOAT! Kobeeeeeeee!!!

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.541
Knights of House Lakers

00:01:27.541 --> 00:01:31.375
tonight we commence what is sure to be a glorious season

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:34.041
the beginning of the end of the long drought.

00:01:34.041 --> 00:01:35.375
Here here!

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.625
For the King of the East now dons the Purple and Gold.

00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:39.875
And together

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:45.041
we will restore the glory of the Greatest House in the Western Realm.

00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:48.500
Now please, eat!

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.041
Especially you, Ingram.

00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:54.500
No, Brandon, you’ve gotta pass to LeBron first now.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.041
Oh, sorry.

00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:03.500
You mustn’t burn your tongue, Your Grace

00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:07.375
So, I hear you’re to be involved in the production of Sea Jam 2.

00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:08.375
Is that correct?

00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:10.250
Uh, yes, that’s right.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.500
Oh, delightful!

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.750
Well, I was thinking, if you’re looking to, say

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.625
reprise Shawn Bradley’s character

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:18.541
I’m a very accomplished Shaqtor...uh...actor.

00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:22.250
You’ll never be clutch like Kobe!

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.750
Who are these clowns?

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:24.875
Kobedicians.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.416
Kobedicians.

00:02:26.416 --> 00:02:29.625
An annoying sect of extremist Kobe fanlings.

00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:31.375
This was done by Lakers fanlings?

00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:32.916
They’re not Laker fans.

00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:34.000
They’re Kobe fans.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.250
They don’t accept LeBron.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.375
They think he’s a soft bitch who can’t play defense.

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:38.500
Watch your tongue, Brandon!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:38.875
What?

00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:40.000
Well, that’s what they say.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.375
LeBron’s a soft bitch.

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:43.041
And he doesn’t play defense.

00:02:43.041 --> 00:02:43.916
See?

00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:44.750
Kobe.

00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:46.791
Alright, let me talk to them.

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:47.750
Don’t bother, LeBron.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.875
You can’t reason with them.

00:02:48.875 --> 00:02:49.875
Just...

00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:50.666
ignore them.

00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:52.541
If I could win back the fanlings
of Cleveland

00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:56.416
I can certainly win the hearts
of a few crazy Kobe fanlings.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:58.625
You can’t make your free throws.

00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:01.750
Good people of Los Angeles.

00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:03.250
Oh shit, it’s LeBron.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:03.750
Booo!

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.625
You suck!

00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:06.000
You’re a stat padder!

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.625
Shh shh, give him a chance,
give him a chance.

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:08.666
Like you

00:03:08.666 --> 00:03:11.125
I have much respect for Kobe. But I—

00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:13.416
Cuz he’s the GOAT

00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:15.000
You’ll never be Kobe, bruv.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.125
I’m not trying to be

00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:17.125
Well, you should.

00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:18.250
Yeah, he’s better than you.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:18.791
Yeah!

00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:19.875
OK.

00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:23.500
Well, is there anything I could
possibly do to win you over?

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.375
I don’t think there’s nothing.

00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:27.125
What if he gave us a billion gold?

00:03:27.125 --> 00:03:27.375
No.

00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:28.500
What if he got “Kobe” tattooed
on his head?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.125
Definitely not.

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:29.375
No.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.500
Maybe 100 championships?

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.000
Six?

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.375
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:31.375 --> 00:03:32.125
Five?

00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:32.625
Eight?

00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:34.375
Go with that. Go with that.

00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:35.500
Yes.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.666
OK?

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:38.250
You gotta win, uh

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.541
six championships.

00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:40.291
Yeah, yeah, six.

00:03:40.291 --> 00:03:40.875
Six, yeah!

00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:41.375
Yeah, yeah—no, seven!

00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:41.916
Seven!

00:03:41.916 --> 00:03:42.375
Six!

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:43.625
What?

00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:45.500
You realize Kobe only won five.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.000
Yeah, but he’s a closer, bitch!

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:47.875
He finishes!

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:49.500
I finish!

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.916
According to the analytics maesters

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:52.875
I’m actually more clutch than Kobe.

00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:54.416
Nah, Kobe’s a killer.

00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:55.500
Like a mambaaa!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.041
Hiss!!

00:03:56.041 --> 00:03:57.375
Well, I built a school!

00:03:57.375 --> 00:03:58.375
Wow!

00:03:58.375 --> 00:03:59.750
Oh, you built a school!

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.125
Yeah, that’s 'cause you’re soft!

00:04:01.125 --> 00:04:02.541
Yeah!

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.625
You have nothing to prove to these fools.

00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:07.041
They’re just a few nuts living in their parents’ barns.

00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:08.666
They’ll come around. Believe me.

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:15.500
Real Kobe fans will NEVER accept LeBron.

00:04:15.541 --> 00:04:16.541
Yeah!

00:04:16.541 --> 00:04:19.125
He doesn’t have the Mamba Mentality.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.625
Yeah!

00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:23.375
Kobe never missed a game-winner!

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:24.625
Yeah!

00:04:24.625 --> 00:04:29.250
I have dedicated my life to the worship of Kobe.

00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:34.500
And I would rather die than worship the false goat LeBron!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.416
Yeah!

00:04:35.416 --> 00:04:42.000
Dominate! Dominate! Dominate!

00:05:20.041 --> 00:05:23.291
Any update on the Jimmy...situation?

00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:27.541
Handled, my liege

00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:31.250
He is in good spirits and should
be returning to practice today

00:05:31.666 --> 00:05:35.125
Oh...so he no longer wants to be traded?

00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:38.458
Um...well...uh...we're working...ya know...

00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:40.791
Who wants to DIE today???

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.541
Ah, that must be him now

00:05:43.291 --> 00:05:44.666
KAT, do something!

00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:47.500
Don’t worry. He can’t do shit against me.

00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:50.541
I hope that means you worked on your defense

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.375
I’ll take those two G Realm peasants,

00:05:53.375 --> 00:05:55.000
the muffin maker’s boy

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.416
and that there mangy goat.

00:05:57.416 --> 00:06:01.875
When they mop whatever’s left of you lily-livered cowards off the court,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.000
they’ll wish they traded me sooner!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.583
He doesn’t seem very happy

00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:09.000
Oh, that's just Jimmy

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.583
Gotta love the intensity he brings...even to practice

00:06:12.583 --> 00:06:13.750
Hallelujah, Wiggins!

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:16.083
Should I send your bones to your brother???

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.000
No! Please, no!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.333
You f--king need me!

00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:21.208
Ah!!!

00:06:21.208 --> 00:06:24.125
Thibby, I just don’t have the stomach for this

00:06:24.125 --> 00:06:25.666
This is the best practice all year

00:06:25.666 --> 00:06:27.375
Jimmy! Here! The Muffin Boy! I’m open!

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:29.375
He’s motivating them

00:06:29.375 --> 00:06:32.416
We yield! We yield! Stop! Stop it, please!

00:06:32.416 --> 00:06:35.333
Aw, seems I’ve found the Towns Crier

00:06:35.333 --> 00:06:37.541
Hahaha!!!

00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:39.833
He’s slaughtering my little Timberpups

00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:42.541
Oh, this was supposed to be our year!

00:06:42.541 --> 00:06:45.541
Hey you, get me a f--king salad! Balsamic dressing

00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:48.833
Actually, no dressing. I’ll use this.

00:06:49.958 --> 00:06:52.166
-Oh, dear god
-You just got served muffins and milk!

00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:53.291
As we said at House Bulls,

00:06:53.291 --> 00:06:56.666
if you’re not mortally wounded, you can still play 48 minutes.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.000
Oh my goodness, is that Andrew’s heart?

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:01.791
Nay. That’s too big.

00:07:02.458 --> 00:07:04.666
Pardon me, uh, have you seen my heart?

00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:06.208
Not now, Andrew!

00:07:06.375 --> 00:07:09.833
Thomas, it might be time to admit this situation is untenable

00:07:09.833 --> 00:07:12.708
What? It’s tenable. It's very tenable.

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:17.416
It’s one of the most tenable situations I have ever...

00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:18.625
tended over

00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:21.625
Curse these forsaken Twin Cities!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:22.916
TRADE ME!

00:07:22.916 --> 00:07:25.916
Remember, last season we were
a 3 seed before he got hurt

00:07:26.125 --> 00:07:28.166
Curse this wretched house!

00:07:28.541 --> 00:07:29.458
TRADE ME!

00:07:29.458 --> 00:07:33.541
I swear this will all work out just fine if we’re just patient—

00:07:33.541 --> 00:07:35.625
And f--k you, Lord Thibodeau!

00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:38.416
Your rotations are shit!

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.791
Well, I do suppose I like Robert Covington’s hustle

00:07:45.208 --> 00:07:47.708
Oh, how exciting is this, Lord Commander?

00:07:47.708 --> 00:07:51.791
Jimmy can take us over the top! He could change everything with his intensity!

00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:53.125
Oh, here he comes now!

00:07:54.083 --> 00:07:56.083
Is that a mini-carriage?

00:07:56.083 --> 00:07:58.041
He sure does have a lot of baggage

00:07:58.125 --> 00:08:00.500
Um...I’d like to be traded, please

00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:10.291
Hello, city of Brotherly Love!!!

00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:13.458
Shall we complete this process now?

00:08:28.208 --> 00:08:30.000
Sometimes I like to pretend

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.375
that I’m King James.

00:08:32.125 --> 00:08:34.333
Blessed by the gods to choose my army,

00:08:34.625 --> 00:08:35.708
my Lord Commander

00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:36.958
and my home

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.500
But alas, I am not

00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:42.000
I am Ser MarShon Brooks

00:08:42.208 --> 00:08:45.125
A journeyman sellsword, who, not long ago,

00:08:45.125 --> 00:08:47.708
was fighting in the distant lands of Chai'Nos,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.583
spending years reassembling

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:51.250
what remained of my shattered spirit

00:08:51.583 --> 00:08:52.958
only to land a seat

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:54.958
on the dreary benches of Memphis.

00:08:56.125 --> 00:08:58.333
But fate is a curious thing

00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:00.083
For yesterday,

00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:02.833
House Suns requested MY services and offered

00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.458
REAL assets in return

00:09:04.458 --> 00:09:07.458
Ser Trevor Ariza AND picks!

00:09:07.833 --> 00:09:09.500
Seems I shall finally prove to everyone

00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:11.958
that I AM a knight worthy of minutes.

00:09:11.958 --> 00:09:14.958
And what I once feared was my twilight

00:09:14.958 --> 00:09:16.083
was in fact,

00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:17.958
my dawn.

00:09:19.875 --> 00:09:21.708
Welcome to House Suns

00:09:21.958 --> 00:09:22.500
Thank you

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.500
Ser MarShon Brooks at your service

00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:26.375
Wait. MarShon Brooks?

00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:27.083
Yes...at your—

00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:28.583
OK, we traded for Dillon Brooks

00:09:28.583 --> 00:09:30.208
You wha—oh, um…

00:09:30.208 --> 00:09:31.708
Dammit, they sent the wrong Br--

00:09:31.708 --> 00:09:33.333
House Grizzlies sent the wrong Brooks

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:34.625
Are you bloody serious?

00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:38.000
Oh, how the fickle tides of fate recede

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.958
as quickly as they crash upon my shores.

00:09:40.333 --> 00:09:43.000
And though my sand castles may wither and wash

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.458
the deft hands of hope must

00:09:44.458 --> 00:09:45.958
always be there to rebuild them.

00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:49.125
I return to Memphis with fresh perspective,

00:09:49.125 --> 00:09:50.500
renewed spirit

00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:58.375
Dearest Jennifer,

00:09:58.375 --> 00:09:59.875
I have received your raven,

00:09:59.875 --> 00:10:01.833
and I beseech you understand.

00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:03.458
I am trying

00:10:03.458 --> 00:10:04.625
I tryeth every day

00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:06.583
to bring you the ring you so desire…

00:10:06.583 --> 00:10:07.625
Watch it. Hey, hey.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:11.208
Look who we blocked coming down the lane

00:10:12.458 --> 00:10:13.458
Well, look who it is!

00:10:13.458 --> 00:10:15.000
The Boogie Knight himself

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.833
They say our bigs can’t defend

00:10:16.833 --> 00:10:18.833
Please! I’ve got a torn Achilles

00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:19.833
Oh, OK

00:10:19.833 --> 00:10:21.333
Last I saw this lot,

00:10:21.333 --> 00:10:22.833
you all were getting swept away

00:10:22.833 --> 00:10:25.833
faster than a harassment case at House Mavericks.

00:10:25.833 --> 00:10:26.958
Oh please, Boogie

00:10:26.958 --> 00:10:28.708
regale us with the tales of

00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:32.083
your extensive tournament experience.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.958
Better none than yours

00:10:34.708 --> 00:10:36.208
Don’t let him get in your head

00:10:36.208 --> 00:10:36.958
Aw...

00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:39.958
Good on you all for giving Jimmer another shot

00:10:39.958 --> 00:10:41.333
What? No. I’m Nik—

00:10:41.333 --> 00:10:41.958
Wait

00:10:41.958 --> 00:10:44.500
I’m not going to fall for your hurtful tricks anymore!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.333
You see, it seems the tables have turned!

00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:49.333
Unlike you, I have two good Achilles AND friends

00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:50.250
We got your back, Nik!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.125
How do you like my sauce now?

00:10:52.125 --> 00:10:52.625
Bitch

00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:55.708
What a fellowship you all have

00:10:55.708 --> 00:10:58.708
Almost makes up for the lack of rings

00:10:58.958 --> 00:10:59.833
The Lord of Light...

00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:01.458
Hearted Locker Room Chemistry

00:11:01.458 --> 00:11:03.083
smiles upon our Brotherhood.

00:11:03.083 --> 00:11:05.208
Who smiles upon you, Boogie?

00:11:05.208 --> 00:11:07.458
You’ve got no rings and no friends

00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:09.583
And which of those can you offer me?

00:11:11.083 --> 00:11:11.750
Friends

00:11:13.625 --> 00:11:15.125
I’d prefer rings

00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:16.708
Well then join us! And together

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:18.875
we shall make it past the second round.

00:11:18.875 --> 00:11:19.375
Whoa, whoa

00:11:19.375 --> 00:11:20.583
I don’t want this guy here

00:11:20.583 --> 00:11:22.250
He’s like, uh, mess with our flow

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:22.958
you know what I mean?

00:11:22.958 --> 00:11:24.500
We have like, uh, good vibes and also

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.375
like, um, we have same agent

00:11:26.375 --> 00:11:28.208
and he says it might affect my minutes.

00:11:28.208 --> 00:11:28.875
Doesn’t matter

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.333
It’s water under the Bay Bridge

00:11:31.333 --> 00:11:33.208
I’m signing with House Warriors

00:11:33.208 --> 00:11:35.125
What? No, you can’t—

00:11:35.125 --> 00:11:36.208
They’re like an All-Star House

00:11:36.208 --> 00:11:37.125
That’s not fair!

00:11:37.125 --> 00:11:37.750
That’ll ruin the Realm!

00:11:37.875 --> 00:11:38.958
He’s full of it

00:11:38.958 --> 00:11:41.958
Everybody knows House Warriors is over the gold cap

00:11:41.958 --> 00:11:44.083
They can’t afford you!

00:11:44.083 --> 00:11:45.458
No, it’s probably mid-level exception

00:11:45.458 --> 00:11:46.750
-Yeah, it’s a mid-level exception
-Yeah, you’ve got the mid-level taxpayers

00:11:46.958 --> 00:11:49.250
Oh right, right. The mid-level exception...

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.750
I of course know what that is

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.250
and fully understand it.

00:11:52.333 --> 00:11:54.583
My mind is a buzzin’

00:11:54.583 --> 00:11:56.458
For I heard a hot take.

00:11:56.458 --> 00:11:58.708
Seems big Boogie Cousins

00:11:58.708 --> 00:12:00.583
Turned into a SNAKE!

00:12:00.583 --> 00:12:02.583
He rides to the Oak Lands

00:12:02.583 --> 00:12:04.333
Where there’s rings all around.

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:06.083
Give his headband a rebrand

00:12:06.083 --> 00:12:08.833
As a ring-chaser’s crown.

00:12:09.583 --> 00:12:11.583
Oh yes! I love Four Bar Fridays!

00:12:11.958 --> 00:12:12.625
Boogie

00:12:12.833 --> 00:12:13.458
Dame

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.083
The only thing more hopeless than

00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:18.500
this brotherhood is your bard career.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.083
-Hey now
-Watch your tongue, Boogie!

00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:21.875
You know, I expect you to be a bastard

00:12:21.875 --> 00:12:23.625
but a coward too?

00:12:23.875 --> 00:12:26.083
I’d rather die than share the court with Curry!

00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:26.583
Um…

00:12:26.583 --> 00:12:28.083
No, sorry—I mean the good—

00:12:28.333 --> 00:12:29.750
I mean Steph

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:31.625
And the rest of those serpents.

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:34.125
Dame, we’ve got no chance!

00:12:34.125 --> 00:12:35.708
We had no chance

00:12:35.708 --> 00:12:36.708
But we do now

00:12:37.208 --> 00:12:40.083
The Lord of Light-Hearted Chemistry is very powerful

00:12:40.083 --> 00:12:42.000
To the humble, He giveth…

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.500
But to the greedy,

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.750
He taketh away.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.458
The Warriors’ defeat can only come from within

00:12:48.125 --> 00:12:50.875
No House can bear the likes of Draymond, KD

00:12:50.875 --> 00:12:51.833
AND Cousins.

00:12:52.333 --> 00:12:54.583
Their golden cup runneth over with assholes

00:12:55.625 --> 00:12:56.458
Let him go

00:12:58.125 --> 00:12:59.958
Hope you enjoy the regular season

00:12:59.958 --> 00:13:01.250
you f--kin’ losers!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.958
I hope you get the f--king eighth seed

00:13:03.958 --> 00:13:06.958
so I can see your faces when we sweep you again!

00:13:07.083 --> 00:13:09.583
I’ll crush you like I crush my Lord Commanders!

00:13:09.583 --> 00:13:11.333
Does he know the way out of here?

00:13:11.333 --> 00:13:14.000
He’ll get himself ejected eventually

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.833
My mind is a buzzin’

00:13:15.833 --> 00:13:17.958
For I heard a hot take.

00:13:17.958 --> 00:13:20.000
Seems big Boogie Cousins

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.208
Turned into a SNAKE!

00:13:22.208 --> 00:13:24.500
He rides to the Oak Lands

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.458
Where there’s rings all around.

00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:28.708
Give his headband a rebrand

00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:31.208
As a ring-chaser’s crown

00:13:32.958 --> 00:13:34.958
A raven has brought us

00:13:34.958 --> 00:13:36.958
some news that is good.

00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:41.375
House Blazers acquired the knight Rodney Hood

00:13:41.375 --> 00:13:45.500
My Rip City brethren, rejoice and give cheer

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.708
Except for Nik Stauskas,

00:13:47.708 --> 00:13:49.750
you’re now a Cavalier.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:50.458
Wait, what?

00:13:50.458 --> 00:13:52.083
Bye, Nik!

00:13:52.083 --> 00:13:53.833
Good luck in Cleveland, Nik!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.500
See, look here, DeMar

00:14:04.875 --> 00:14:06.000
Draymond’s on LeBron again...

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
Yeah, it’s like a triple switch or something

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:08.500
Exactly...

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.250
What are you reading?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.875
We’re studying.

00:14:10.875 --> 00:14:13.541
House Warriors' defensive tactics against King James

00:14:13.541 --> 00:14:15.375
It wasn’t their tactics.

00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:16.416
It was their talent.

00:14:16.416 --> 00:14:17.541
We have the talent.

00:14:17.541 --> 00:14:19.125
We just need smart strategy

00:14:19.125 --> 00:14:21.125
and for the gods to finally smile on us.

00:14:21.125 --> 00:14:22.541
Maybe they have

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.750
DeMar! This is our chance!

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.041
King James is gone from our path,

00:14:28.041 --> 00:14:30.416
but he is also gone from our excuses.

00:14:30.416 --> 00:14:32.750
If we fail to conquer the East this year…

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.375
it could be the end for all of us.

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:37.125
My lord, you have always believed in us

00:14:37.125 --> 00:14:39.166
We will reward your faith. I swear it

00:14:41.625 --> 00:14:43.625
I’m afraid faith is not enough

00:14:44.375 --> 00:14:47.000
Here we pay a Northern price for a blessing

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.125
The gods demand a sacrifice

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.875
Lord Ujiri, I pledge that I will do whatever it takes

00:14:53.875 --> 00:14:56.000
Yes. We’d give anything for The Six

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:56.875
I know

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.041
Forgive me

00:15:06.416 --> 00:15:08.291
Kyle! Wake up! Kyle! Kyle!

00:15:08.291 --> 00:15:09.291
Norman?

00:15:09.291 --> 00:15:09.916
What are you doing—

00:15:09.916 --> 00:15:11.750
It’s a trade. We’re making a trade.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:12.500
A trade?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.000
Why didn’t anyone tell me?

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:14.750
Well...you know...

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:16.375
you did trade for a horse once...

00:15:16.375 --> 00:15:18.041
and I think Lord Ujiri doesn’t include you

00:15:18.041 --> 00:15:19.375
Ugh! He’s so annoying!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.250
Excuse me. Excuse me!

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:23.625
Get out of my way

00:15:24.041 --> 00:15:25.500
No...no...no...

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:26.250
Kyle!

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.625
Don’t let them do it

00:15:27.625 --> 00:15:28.250
I won’t

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.916
This must be some sort of mistake—

00:15:29.916 --> 00:15:33.500
He was here for a long time, not a good time

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.625
What? Where’s Lord Ujiri?

00:15:35.625 --> 00:15:37.000
It will all be over soon

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.750
No! I demand to see Lord Ujiri!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.750
Where is Lord Ujiri???

00:15:41.291 --> 00:15:43.125
My Lord…you can’t!

00:15:43.125 --> 00:15:44.416
You said you wouldn’t!

00:15:44.416 --> 00:15:45.250
Gods’ plan

00:15:46.875 --> 00:15:48.375
Drake, have you all gone mad?

00:15:48.375 --> 00:15:49.750
If we don’t make a trade,

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:51.250
there will be no banners here.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.000
Oh, is that what they said at House Thunder

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.416
when they traded away James Harden?

00:15:54.416 --> 00:15:55.791
Ah, man. That’s not the same!

00:15:55.791 --> 00:15:58.750
Silver Lord, bless this trade,

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:01.250
for it is fair and for the good of the Realm!

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.416
How could you do this to your most loyal knight?

00:16:03.416 --> 00:16:04.750
Not just him

00:16:05.041 --> 00:16:08.625
Also Jake—Jakob…Pole-tull...

00:16:08.625 --> 00:16:12.791
Po-ull-tull... Poyttle... Pelt-el...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.625
Him!

00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:16.000
Hello!

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:20.500
All right, summon the Trade Raptor!

00:16:47.125 --> 00:16:50.875
Ah! Ah! Ahhh!! No! Noooo!!!!

00:16:50.875 --> 00:16:52.291
Bye, Jacob Poortle!

00:16:52.291 --> 00:16:53.750
It's Jakob Poeltl

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.625
Please. I’ll do whatever you ask.

00:16:55.625 --> 00:16:56.750
I’ll shoot more threes!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.166
Lord Ujiri! How could you do this?

00:16:59.166 --> 00:17:00.500
He’s my best friend!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.625
It’s OK. I’ll be your new best friend.

00:17:02.625 --> 00:17:03.541
Shush, Norman!

00:17:03.541 --> 00:17:05.416
Kyle...please

00:17:05.416 --> 00:17:07.000
Is there any other way?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
We tried. They didn’t want you.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.000
Please! Please! I'll try on defense!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.375
I’ll shoot it from anywhere

00:17:13.375 --> 00:17:15.750
I’ll shoot it from behind half court

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:18.375
No! No! No! No! Please! Please!

00:17:21.541 --> 00:17:22.250
Hi, DeMar!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.416
Oh, hi, Jakob

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.375
Wait…WAIT. WAIT!

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.916
I almost forgot

00:17:31.625 --> 00:17:33.666
We also owe them a first-round pick

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:35.750
Ow. Oh, come on

00:17:35.875 --> 00:17:37.500
OK. We’re good. We should be good

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.875
Trade Raptor, take these knights to their new house

00:17:40.875 --> 00:17:43.250
Wait. DeMar AND a pick?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.750
And Jake Puddle

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.166
Argh, get off me!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.250
No! Please, come back! No!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.000
My friend...

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.625
Well, whoever we’re getting back…

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.291
he’d better be a bloody monster!

00:18:21.708 --> 00:18:23.750
So the key here again is spacing.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:25.083
I need you in the corner,

00:18:25.083 --> 00:18:27.208
and if your man so much as looks my way,

00:18:27.208 --> 00:18:28.250
then I’m going to get it to you.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.500
Then I go up for three.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.375
Yes.

00:18:30.375 --> 00:18:31.250
But 'tis merely a pump fake!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:31.833
No

00:18:31.833 --> 00:18:32.708
I pull the ball down!

00:18:32.708 --> 00:18:33.875
I step over the line.

00:18:33.875 --> 00:18:34.250
No

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:34.875
I back down the big for

00:18:34.875 --> 00:18:36.625
a contested fadeaway two from the elbow.

00:18:36.625 --> 00:18:38.875
No. That’s exactly what you shouldn’t do

00:18:38.875 --> 00:18:40.500
Chris, you know I can hit that shot over anybody

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.000
All day

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.250
It’s not about hitting shots

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.875
It’s about hitting EFFICIENT shots

00:18:43.875 --> 00:18:46.125
Ugh, not you too with this efficiency fad

00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:47.208
Whatever happened to the days when

00:18:47.208 --> 00:18:49.625
knights would go one-on-one, mano-y-mano

00:18:49.625 --> 00:18:52.625
in the paint, in a slow, grinding duel?

00:18:52.625 --> 00:18:53.583
Melo...

00:18:53.583 --> 00:18:55.375
if you want a role here on House Rockets

00:18:55.375 --> 00:18:57.000
you must understand the system.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.583
Study the analytics

00:18:58.583 --> 00:18:59.583
I study plenty!

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:02.833
Carmelo, please

00:19:02.833 --> 00:19:04.500
I remember when you used to be fun!

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.208
Whatever happened to Banana Boat Chris?

00:19:06.208 --> 00:19:07.583
He learned how to win

00:19:07.583 --> 00:19:08.708
And he wants to teach his friend,

00:19:08.708 --> 00:19:09.958
so they can win together.

00:19:09.958 --> 00:19:11.208
I want to win…it’s just…

00:19:11.208 --> 00:19:13.083
it’s all so boring these days

00:19:13.083 --> 00:19:15.750
Analytics, efficiency, defense...

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.750
Hm, you know what? Come with me.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.500
I want to show you something

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.375
Whoa

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.625
Ah, Carmelo!

00:19:31.625 --> 00:19:33.833
Welcome to the Johnson Spacing Center

00:19:33.833 --> 00:19:36.208
Here, our Maesters test the frontiers of knowledge

00:19:36.208 --> 00:19:37.875
to give House Rockets a competitive edge

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.250
What’s that?

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.375
Why, that’s our namesake. The rocket.

00:19:41.375 --> 00:19:43.208
We value long-range weaponry here

00:19:43.208 --> 00:19:46.000
House Rockets has never shied away from experimentation

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.875
Some produce incredible results

00:19:47.875 --> 00:19:49.375
And others….

00:19:49.375 --> 00:19:50.125
not so much.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.125
What is this for?

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.625
Ah, that was Yao Ming’s chamber pot

00:19:57.375 --> 00:19:59.458
Melo, have a look at this

00:20:00.958 --> 00:20:02.000
What is that?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.333
Those are moons orbiting another world

00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:05.958
Makes you think...

00:20:05.958 --> 00:20:08.750
you might not be the center of the universe after all

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.833
Huh, so you’re saying I’m just another planet?

00:20:10.833 --> 00:20:13.375
No. He’s saying you are a moon

00:20:13.375 --> 00:20:16.000
James Harden is the planet

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.375
Well, actually, Chris,

00:20:17.375 --> 00:20:18.958
I am a star.

00:20:18.958 --> 00:20:22.625
And stars should be STARters

00:20:22.625 --> 00:20:23.333
Melo

00:20:23.333 --> 00:20:25.000
...just needs a headband

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.125
And I’m gonna put a hoodie here

00:20:26.125 --> 00:20:27.125
Melo, you’re not getting it—

00:20:27.125 --> 00:20:29.458
You know, I bet the only reason I’m not starting

00:20:29.458 --> 00:20:32.250
is because D’Antoni’s still bitter about New York.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.125
No, no, no...

00:20:33.125 --> 00:20:34.833
he’s just working off the Model

00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:36.208
The Model?

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.000
It’s not possible

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.708
I can’t just shoot 30 threes a game

00:20:39.708 --> 00:20:40.875
Look right here, James.

00:20:40.875 --> 00:20:43.500
If the Model is correct, you could TRIPLE your offense

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.125
and pull us out of this slump

00:20:45.125 --> 00:20:46.625
But what if I miss them?

00:20:46.625 --> 00:20:48.375
I could go 0-for-27 myself!

00:20:48.375 --> 00:20:49.875
Ah, but James…

00:20:49.875 --> 00:20:51.375
what if you make them?

00:20:54.125 --> 00:20:55.083
Aagh! What the— Carmelo?

00:20:55.083 --> 00:20:56.125
What are you doing here?

00:20:56.125 --> 00:20:57.833
Carmelo is interested in the Model

00:20:57.833 --> 00:21:00.875
Really? Analytics? Melo?

00:21:00.875 --> 00:21:01.750
OK...

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.875
This is the Model

00:21:04.875 --> 00:21:07.875
We feed her data, and she gives us answers

00:21:07.875 --> 00:21:10.083
untainted by human bias.

00:21:11.125 --> 00:21:12.625
Huh, why does she have six arms?

00:21:12.625 --> 00:21:14.083
...And four boobs?

00:21:14.083 --> 00:21:15.958
Well, she was designed by a bunch of nerds who,

00:21:15.958 --> 00:21:18.500
let’s just say...haven’t had too much experience

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.125
with the anatomy of a female

00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:22.125
Carmelo, you have to understand this machine

00:21:22.125 --> 00:21:23.875
it...doesn’t care about your feelings

00:21:23.875 --> 00:21:26.708
The Model only knows pure analytics

00:21:26.708 --> 00:21:28.625
If this thing truly knows basketball,

00:21:28.625 --> 00:21:30.000
then I should have nothing to fear.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.333
Show me how it works

00:21:31.333 --> 00:21:34.125
These are your career stats. Let’s feed them in.

00:21:35.208 --> 00:21:36.875
Hope she likes empty calories

00:21:44.083 --> 00:21:45.708
OK. Model...

00:21:45.708 --> 00:21:48.958
should Ser Carmelo be in the Hall of Fame?

00:21:50.375 --> 00:21:52.625
Ah, look at that. First ballot

00:21:52.958 --> 00:21:53.833
Brilliant.

00:21:53.833 --> 00:21:56.000
Now, I want to know what my role here should be

00:21:56.583 --> 00:21:57.375
May I?

00:21:57.375 --> 00:21:58.875
Oh, uh, sure! Take it away

00:21:59.458 --> 00:22:00.250
Model...

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.333
what should be my role on House Rockets?

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:13.000
He should’ve dunked that. He had the lane.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.875
This Model is nothing but a hater!

00:22:14.875 --> 00:22:16.333
How does this bloody thing even work?

00:22:16.333 --> 00:22:17.500
Don’t, Carmelo

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.125
That’s where the computers are

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:21.458
Computers? What’s a computer?

00:22:21.458 --> 00:22:23.125
Melo, don't—oh

00:22:23.125 --> 00:22:25.250
The computers do all the calculations

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:26.375
needed to run the Model.

00:22:26.375 --> 00:22:27.500
Oh, do they?

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:29.708
Well, do any of you even watch basketball?!

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:32.875
You don’t have a good VORP

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:36.458
W-why—what’s with their eyes?!

00:22:36.458 --> 00:22:37.875
These poor souls witnessed

00:22:37.875 --> 00:22:40.625
the dark ages of basketball in the early aughts.

00:22:40.625 --> 00:22:43.000
The endless post plays. The long twos.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.125
Ser Jordan on the Wizards

00:22:45.125 --> 00:22:47.750
After a second Finals appearance by House Nets,

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:49.750
they couldn’t bear it any longer.

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:51.500
They gouged out their eyes

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:52.750
But on a positive note,

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.000
it turns out they’re perfect

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:55.625
for doing double-blinded analytics

00:22:55.625 --> 00:22:57.375
Many became computers

00:22:57.375 --> 00:22:58.875
The rest became referees

00:23:00.875 --> 00:23:02.583
I don’t like your true shooting...

00:23:02.583 --> 00:23:04.375
All right. Well, we really should get going, though.

00:23:04.375 --> 00:23:06.583
You’re beginning to taint their judgment

00:23:06.583 --> 00:23:08.458
Oh, you feel taller in person

00:23:08.458 --> 00:23:09.083
Get off me!

00:23:09.083 --> 00:23:11.625
Ser Carmelo, can you sign my abacus?

00:23:11.625 --> 00:23:13.208
-No! I need to get out of here
-Nice boots! I like your boots

00:23:13.208 --> 00:23:14.625
This is madness!

00:23:14.625 --> 00:23:16.875
Well if you’d settle your emotional response,

00:23:16.875 --> 00:23:18.583
you’d see it’s all quite logical, really.

00:23:18.583 --> 00:23:20.083
No...no…this is all wrong

00:23:20.083 --> 00:23:22.000
Your cold, heartless numbers

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.875
know nothing of my value

00:23:23.875 --> 00:23:25.000
Anyone with eyes

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.708
can see the beauty of my game

00:23:26.708 --> 00:23:28.625
A 10-time All-Star

00:23:28.625 --> 00:23:30.875
behind PJ Tucker, really?

00:23:30.875 --> 00:23:32.125
Marquese Chriss, actually—

00:23:32.125 --> 00:23:35.125
Well I refuse to accept it, and I’ll never accept it!

00:23:35.125 --> 00:23:36.708
Why did you even bring me here?!

00:23:36.708 --> 00:23:38.875
Because you’re worth the risk…

00:23:38.875 --> 00:23:40.250
at the veteran minimum

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:42.250
Carmelo, Lord Morey has given you a chance,

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:44.000
and it may be the only one you have left

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:45.708
Well, that’s ridiculous. I just need the ball.

00:23:45.708 --> 00:23:48.000
I can still take any knight one-on-one!

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:49.250
Just give me the rock and I’ll—

00:23:53.625 --> 00:23:55.625
Oh, what. C’mon, he f--ked me in New York

00:23:59.958 --> 00:24:01.458
Hm...interesting

00:24:01.458 --> 00:24:03.333
Oh, Seven Hells...Austin Rivers?

00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:16.625
I can’t wait to share the court with you and

00:24:16.625 --> 00:24:19.416
the legendary Ser Dirk.

00:24:20.416 --> 00:24:21.625
Would you like to see him?

00:24:21.625 --> 00:24:22.666
Is he...uh...

00:24:22.666 --> 00:24:23.583
you know...is he like, uh...

00:24:23.583 --> 00:24:25.583
His, uh, spirit is strong,

00:24:25.583 --> 00:24:28.541
but I am afraid there is not much time left.

00:24:28.541 --> 00:24:29.416
OK

00:24:29.416 --> 00:24:30.833
He’s down to 10 minutes a battle

00:24:30.833 --> 00:24:31.750
Oh my

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:34.083
But come, you will make him very happy

00:24:35.416 --> 00:24:36.708
Ser Dirk, remember:

00:24:36.708 --> 00:24:40.375
You can fight for this house for as long as you like

00:24:40.375 --> 00:24:43.375
Danke, but I don’t have much left...

00:24:43.375 --> 00:24:46.125
maybe only...six seasons or something

00:24:46.125 --> 00:24:47.625
Six?!

00:24:47.625 --> 00:24:50.375
That’s fine...that’s totally fine

00:24:50.375 --> 00:24:53.250
Is, uh, now a good time? Ser Kristaps is here to see—

00:24:53.250 --> 00:24:54.291
Oh yes, yes!

00:24:54.291 --> 00:24:57.208
Dirk, someone special wants to see you

00:24:57.208 --> 00:24:59.625
Hello, my Euro father

00:24:59.625 --> 00:25:01.875
You shaved your beard, Tyson

00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:04.208
-Oh, that’s not Tyson, Dirk. It’s Kristaps!
-It is not him

00:25:04.208 --> 00:25:06.875
Oh! Kristaps?

00:25:06.875 --> 00:25:08.666
You’re...you’re on House Mavericks?

00:25:08.666 --> 00:25:09.666
I am, yeah

00:25:09.666 --> 00:25:13.583
Lord Mark, this is...truly a wonderful gift

00:25:13.583 --> 00:25:14.625
Oh, it’s nothing

00:25:14.625 --> 00:25:16.250
Almost makes up for...

00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:18.375
the time I took a giant pay cut...

00:25:18.375 --> 00:25:19.125
OK

00:25:19.125 --> 00:25:20.666
to stay with House Mavs...

00:25:20.666 --> 00:25:21.750
OK, we don't need to rehash the whole—

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:23.500
and you used the gold on...

00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:24.583
Chandler Parsons.

00:25:24.583 --> 00:25:25.458
Alright, OK

00:25:25.458 --> 00:25:26.916
Not good

00:25:26.916 --> 00:25:29.625
OK, well, I will let you boys alone to talk about

00:25:29.625 --> 00:25:31.416
whatever European things you guys wanna talk about

00:25:31.416 --> 00:25:34.041
like wine and bread and cheese.

00:25:34.041 --> 00:25:36.750
I get it. All right. Later, dudes!

00:25:36.750 --> 00:25:38.916
Mark is actually...

00:25:38.916 --> 00:25:40.416
He’s a very cool guy

00:25:40.416 --> 00:25:43.375
Your grace, I want to learn everything you have to teach me

00:25:43.375 --> 00:25:45.708
Let me bask in the light of your wisdom

00:25:45.708 --> 00:25:49.583
I will tell you what is the most important

00:25:49.583 --> 00:25:50.750
Yes. Please.

00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:52.458
Loyalty

00:25:52.458 --> 00:25:57.458
For 56 years, I have worn only House Mavericks colors,

00:25:57.458 --> 00:26:00.125
even as those colors went through

00:26:00.125 --> 00:26:01.916
a questionable rebrand.

00:26:01.916 --> 00:26:05.000
And though I showed my opponents no mercy,

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:09.250
I made no enemies because I betrayed no house

00:26:09.250 --> 00:26:10.250
Tell me,

00:26:10.250 --> 00:26:14.708
why did you abandon your house? Your fanlings?

00:26:14.708 --> 00:26:17.708
Well...I was on House Knicks, and—

00:26:17.708 --> 00:26:18.541
Oh, oh—say no more

00:26:18.541 --> 00:26:21.125
OK, yikes, yikes. Never mind.

00:26:21.125 --> 00:26:23.541
Kristaps, do you then swear

00:26:23.541 --> 00:26:27.500
your loyalty to House Mavericks?

00:26:27.500 --> 00:26:28.750
Yes, I do

00:26:28.750 --> 00:26:29.750
Well then,

00:26:29.750 --> 00:26:33.541
in the name of Dirk Nowitzki of House Mavericks,

00:26:33.541 --> 00:26:38.666
I hereby declare you the next Dirk

00:26:38.666 --> 00:26:40.333
OK, wait. Hold on

00:26:40.333 --> 00:26:42.625
With all due respect, you said

00:26:42.625 --> 00:26:44.791
I was the next Dirk, like like a moon ago

00:26:44.791 --> 00:26:47.791
Oh...that’s right. OK, yeah.

00:26:47.791 --> 00:26:51.958
Kristaps, you will be the next Dirk,

00:26:51.958 --> 00:26:54.458
UNTIL Luka comes of age.

00:26:54.458 --> 00:26:57.375
Right...but I’m already the go-to knight, right?

00:26:57.375 --> 00:26:59.250
I’m scoring roughly 20 points a battle

00:27:02.041 --> 00:27:04.958
What if, uh, maybe both of you are the next Dirk?

00:27:04.958 --> 00:27:06.541
We’ll do double Dirks

00:27:06.541 --> 00:27:07.791
Yeah, you can be double Dirks

00:27:07.791 --> 00:27:10.500
Want to be triple Dirks? Could we do triple Dirks?

00:27:10.500 --> 00:27:11.541
Triple Dirks? Who is the other—

00:27:11.541 --> 00:27:16.625
I think I also told Maxi Kleber that he’s the next me

00:27:16.625 --> 00:27:18.708
Ser, our next battle starts in eight hours

00:27:18.708 --> 00:27:19.625
We need to start your stretches

00:27:19.625 --> 00:27:22.291
Oh, dank—thank you, J.J.

00:27:22.291 --> 00:27:24.041
I’ll be right there

00:27:24.708 --> 00:27:26.958
All right, boys

00:27:26.958 --> 00:27:28.625
Time to play some basketball!

00:27:43.958 --> 00:27:45.125
What the hell, Kuz?

00:27:45.125 --> 00:27:46.083
Oh, c’mon,

00:27:46.083 --> 00:27:48.458
probably would have been more off target if I left you alone.

00:27:48.458 --> 00:27:50.500
That arrow cost 200 gold

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:52.166
Who pays 200 gold for—

00:27:52.166 --> 00:27:54.000
Ah, right

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:55.458
Wait, weren't you cutting ties with them?

00:27:55.458 --> 00:27:57.250
Yeah, but I got to get that arrow back

00:27:57.250 --> 00:27:59.000
It's going to be a collector's item

00:28:10.541 --> 00:28:12.166
Oh, you must come to my barbershop

00:28:12.166 --> 00:28:14.666
But I have a barber. He’s an eyebrow specialist

00:28:15.958 --> 00:28:20.458
Hey Lonzo, I’m not sure it’s safe to climb in ZO2 boots!

00:28:20.458 --> 00:28:21.166
If Lord Walton sees you,

00:28:21.166 --> 00:28:23.125
he’ll give Rondo ALL your minutes.

00:28:23.125 --> 00:28:24.875
Shhh! Shut up!

00:28:24.875 --> 00:28:26.791
I want nothing more than to be by your side

00:28:26.791 --> 00:28:28.250
Oh, think of the fast breaks

00:28:28.250 --> 00:28:30.708
I yearn to toss your lobs

00:28:30.708 --> 00:28:32.833
Think of the spacing!

00:28:32.833 --> 00:28:34.041
Would you let me play power forward?

00:28:34.041 --> 00:28:35.083
Yes, anything.

00:28:35.083 --> 00:28:36.708
Even though I’m clearly a center?

00:28:36.708 --> 00:28:39.375
Oh, whatever you want. Because together,

00:28:39.375 --> 00:28:41.000
we will bring back Showtime.

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:43.666
Ugh, too bad Lord Demps would never trade me here

00:28:43.666 --> 00:28:45.208
He just hates House Lakers

00:28:45.208 --> 00:28:46.916
He’s always been jealous of big markets

00:28:46.916 --> 00:28:48.375
Let Rich handle Dell

00:28:48.375 --> 00:28:49.125
But you’d have to give up

00:28:49.125 --> 00:28:51.250
your entire young core for my rights.

00:28:51.250 --> 00:28:53.500
I would trade every single one of them

00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:55.583
for just a chance to play with you.

00:28:55.583 --> 00:28:56.916
Between you and me,

00:28:56.916 --> 00:28:59.375
they’re a bunch of fools and overhyped squires.

00:28:59.375 --> 00:29:00.458
Even the Ball boy?

00:29:00.458 --> 00:29:01.750
Pfft. Lonzo?

00:29:01.750 --> 00:29:05.291
Good riddance to him AND his oaf of a father

00:29:05.291 --> 00:29:06.416
And once he’s gone,

00:29:06.416 --> 00:29:08.125
we'll bring in a real Lord Commander

00:29:08.125 --> 00:29:09.375
like Jason Kidd

00:29:09.375 --> 00:29:11.125
-Wait! Stop! Stop!
-or Mark Jack—son of a—

00:29:12.958 --> 00:29:14.625
Are you completely mad?

00:29:14.625 --> 00:29:16.500
He saw us. He saw us tampering.

00:29:16.500 --> 00:29:18.375
It’s all right. It’s all right. I know.

00:29:19.041 --> 00:29:19.916
What should we do with you?

00:29:19.916 --> 00:29:21.375
D-d-don’t trade me

00:29:21.375 --> 00:29:23.458
I’m really good except for shooting free throws

00:29:23.458 --> 00:29:24.666
and three-pointers

00:29:24.666 --> 00:29:25.083
and layups,

00:29:25.083 --> 00:29:27.041
but, uh...I was the No. 2 pick!

00:29:27.041 --> 00:29:28.541
He was the No. 2 pick

00:29:30.541 --> 00:29:32.500
The things I do for rings

00:29:33.916 --> 00:29:35.416
Ow, ow!

00:29:35.416 --> 00:29:37.500
-Ow, my ankle!
-My small Kevin Durant-like frame!

00:29:38.291 --> 00:29:42.041
Oh, my bones have shattered like sugar straws!

00:29:44.083 --> 00:29:47.083
Oh, come on, guys, shake it off!

00:29:47.083 --> 00:29:48.208
You’re fine!

00:29:48.208 --> 00:29:50.916
Just a little, uh...playoff push

00:29:50.916 --> 00:29:52.625
from the greatest knight in the Realm.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:55.166
Is someone going to help us up?

00:29:55.166 --> 00:29:57.250
Well, I suppose there's always next year

00:29:57.250 --> 00:29:58.958
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. Right.

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:21.291
Welcome to the Sept of Baylor, a shrine to bad front-office decisions,

00:30:21.291 --> 00:30:24.291
the kind that have led all of you here to the draft lottery!

00:30:27.041 --> 00:30:29.875
Today, we gather in the presence of the lottery gods

00:30:29.875 --> 00:30:32.666
to witness the bestowing of the first pick.

00:30:32.666 --> 00:30:36.125
I am Mark Tatum, Hand of the High Commissioner

00:30:36.125 --> 00:30:37.041
Where’s the Silver Lord?

00:30:37.041 --> 00:30:38.916
What, he too good for us?

00:30:38.916 --> 00:30:40.666
Yes, actually. And besides, this is…

00:30:40.666 --> 00:30:42.791
Yes, actually. And besides, this is…

00:30:42.791 --> 00:30:43.750
this is sort of my thing.

00:30:43.750 --> 00:30:44.541
Yeah, you know what?

00:30:44.541 --> 00:30:47.416
Let’s just take a moment to appreciate Mark Tatum

00:30:48.416 --> 00:30:49.916
That’s right!

00:30:49.916 --> 00:30:51.875
Let’s give a little love to the guy behind the guy

00:30:52.166 --> 00:30:53.791
OK all right. Thanks.

00:30:53.791 --> 00:30:58.625
As per tradition, each house has chosen one delegate to represent them

00:30:58.625 --> 00:31:00.916
I do question some of your delegate choices,

00:31:00.916 --> 00:31:03.750
but then again, questionable decisions are why

00:31:03.750 --> 00:31:06.375
many of you find yourselves here.

00:31:06.375 --> 00:31:08.416
Um...House Pelicans...

00:31:08.416 --> 00:31:11.625
Come on, you know who the fanlings want to see

00:31:11.625 --> 00:31:12.916
That’s better

00:31:12.916 --> 00:31:15.416
Um...excuse me, House Mavs?

00:31:15.416 --> 00:31:17.041
What is this?

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:18.791
We’re, uh, Triple Dirks

00:31:18.791 --> 00:31:21.041
OK, well, you gotta pick one representative,

00:31:21.041 --> 00:31:24.166
so figure out who is the next Dirk in the next 10 seconds, please.

00:31:24.166 --> 00:31:27.375
All right, well, I mean, I’m the most experienced…

00:31:27.375 --> 00:31:29.916
Well, I’m clearly the face of House Mavericks

00:31:29.916 --> 00:31:31.916
And I’m from Dirk’s hometown

00:31:31.916 --> 00:31:33.291
so yeah...I mean it’s hard

00:31:33.291 --> 00:31:34.416
We all have really good cases

00:31:34.416 --> 00:31:37.000
All right, you know what? I’ll let you guys sort this out next season

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:38.041
House Lakers?

00:31:38.041 --> 00:31:41.041
-Get out there
-All right. Get off me

00:31:41.916 --> 00:31:43.125
Hi

00:31:43.125 --> 00:31:44.041
Hey

00:31:44.041 --> 00:31:46.166
OK, so, we’re all good?

00:31:46.166 --> 00:31:47.666
Everyone knows how this works?

00:31:47.666 --> 00:31:49.916
Uh...not really

00:31:49.916 --> 00:31:52.666
Right. Well, each house will have a chance to make

00:31:52.666 --> 00:31:54.916
their final plea to the lottery gods as to

00:31:54.916 --> 00:31:57.541
why they should get the first pick.

00:31:57.541 --> 00:32:00.125
So, who would like to be the first to make a claim?

00:32:01.166 --> 00:32:04.375
Great, the goat...made poop on the floor

00:32:04.375 --> 00:32:05.291
Excuse me?

00:32:05.291 --> 00:32:06.166
No, not you

00:32:06.166 --> 00:32:08.291
Sarver, why is there a goat here?

00:32:08.291 --> 00:32:11.166
Because it’s a metaphor and it’s FUNNY

00:32:11.166 --> 00:32:13.666
OK, well, please send a new representative down

00:32:13.666 --> 00:32:15.041
Preferably a human

00:32:15.041 --> 00:32:16.916
OK, the floor is open

00:32:16.916 --> 00:32:19.666
Oh...I’ll take a stab here

00:32:19.666 --> 00:32:21.416
I would say to the gods

00:32:21.416 --> 00:32:24.625
that you should give House Kings the first pick because—

00:32:24.625 --> 00:32:26.916
Actually, no, it would go to the Sixers

00:32:26.916 --> 00:32:29.375
Aw, crap, yeah...

00:32:29.375 --> 00:32:32.916
OK, gods, you should give House Kings the second pick—

00:32:32.916 --> 00:32:35.791
No, then it would go to House Celtics, I believe

00:32:35.791 --> 00:32:38.791
Wait, what? Who made this—I made this

00:32:38.791 --> 00:32:39.791
Ugh

00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:42.541
OK, do some—someone else should go. I don’t want to.

00:32:42.541 --> 00:32:45.541
No house has fallen harder than that of the Grizzly

00:32:45.541 --> 00:32:47.416
Ser Gasol is gone,

00:32:47.416 --> 00:32:51.666
but Chandler Parsons—and his stupid contract—remain

00:32:51.666 --> 00:32:53.000
Eh, could be worse

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:56.916
Bless us, oh lottery gods, with the squire Zion,

00:32:56.916 --> 00:32:59.791
so that Grit and Grind may rise again,

00:32:59.791 --> 00:33:02.625
as a bane to all Western powers.

00:33:02.625 --> 00:33:06.541
The great House Knicks has not had a first pick in over 30 years

00:33:06.541 --> 00:33:07.666
Lord Fizdale?

00:33:07.666 --> 00:33:11.875
We finally have cast off our overrated European big man

00:33:11.875 --> 00:33:14.625
to make room for the Great Zion

00:33:14.625 --> 00:33:17.291
Please, gods, take that for data,

00:33:17.291 --> 00:33:19.666
and give House Knicks the first pick.

00:33:19.666 --> 00:33:20.541
Oh yeah, please

00:33:20.541 --> 00:33:22.000
If House Knicks gets Zion, they’ll just

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.625
send him away in another terrible trade, right?

00:33:24.625 --> 00:33:25.250
Rude!

00:33:25.250 --> 00:33:30.125
You, Ser Kristaps, are now banned from The Garden!

00:33:30.166 --> 00:33:33.166
OK, you can’t just ban an opposing knight from your arena

00:33:33.166 --> 00:33:34.666
You’re banned, Mark!

00:33:34.666 --> 00:33:36.916
Does anyone else want to make a plea to the gods?

00:33:36.916 --> 00:33:39.125
Ah, Ser Devin. Welcome.

00:33:39.125 --> 00:33:40.416
Screw House Suns!

00:33:40.416 --> 00:33:42.166
They rejected our alliance

00:33:42.166 --> 00:33:44.250
and stole the first pick from us last year.

00:33:44.250 --> 00:33:45.500
Yeah, they already have Luka!

00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:46.416
No they don’t

00:33:46.416 --> 00:33:48.750
Wait, so who did you guys take?

00:33:48.750 --> 00:33:49.666
I think Trae Young

00:33:49.666 --> 00:33:51.166
Huh? What?

00:33:51.166 --> 00:33:52.500
We took Deandre Ayton

00:33:52.500 --> 00:33:53.666
Oh, yeah

00:33:53.666 --> 00:33:54.875
How's he been this year?

00:33:54.875 --> 00:33:55.916
He’s actually pretty solid…

00:33:55.916 --> 00:33:56.666
Yeah?

00:33:56.666 --> 00:33:58.791
Uh, yeah, he’s quietly having a decent squire season

00:33:58.791 --> 00:34:00.041
-Oh, that’s good to hear
-You like to hear that

00:34:00.041 --> 00:34:00.916
Ser Anthony Davis?

00:34:00.916 --> 00:34:03.291
You want to make a plea for House Pelicans?

00:34:03.291 --> 00:34:05.166
Yes

00:34:05.166 --> 00:34:08.791
Read this, and we will trade you to House Lakers

00:34:08.791 --> 00:34:10.291
Not that part. Don’t read that part!

00:34:10.291 --> 00:34:13.291
Ah, right. OK, let’s try this again

00:34:13.291 --> 00:34:16.416
We, House Pelicans, are but a humble house,

00:34:16.416 --> 00:34:19.125
and we kindly ask you for your blessing.

00:34:19.125 --> 00:34:22.541
Zion is the hero that House Pelicans needs,

00:34:22.541 --> 00:34:26.291
a knight who can take us further than one playoff series win...

00:34:26.291 --> 00:34:28.041
...in seven seasons.

00:34:28.041 --> 00:34:31.041
We once had a transformative, all-realm knight,

00:34:32.291 --> 00:34:34.666
but he lacked the fortitude to take…

00:34:34.666 --> 00:34:36.500
the fortitude it takes to commit to a small market.

00:34:36.500 --> 00:34:38.916
OK, it’s MY fault? That I—

00:34:38.916 --> 00:34:41.916
Sorry I couldn't beat House Warriors with Jrue Holiday

00:34:41.916 --> 00:34:44.000
and half a season of Boogie Cousins.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:46.416
Um, thank you, AD...

00:34:46.416 --> 00:34:48.750
House Cavs, would you like to make your case?

00:34:48.750 --> 00:34:52.666
If the gods truly care to see the squire Zion flourish,

00:34:52.666 --> 00:34:55.666
they should give the first pick to House Cavs,

00:34:55.666 --> 00:34:59.166
where he will be surrounded by championship-caliber veterans

00:34:59.166 --> 00:35:00.791
and a Lord who knows how to win.

00:35:00.791 --> 00:35:04.750
Oh, please. You know, there’s a reason I left...

00:35:04.750 --> 00:35:05.375
twice.

00:35:05.375 --> 00:35:06.166
Oh yeah?

00:35:06.166 --> 00:35:07.916
Because you’ve made House Lakers such

00:35:07.916 --> 00:35:09.916
a welcoming place for young talent?

00:35:09.916 --> 00:35:11.541
Who's fitting out now?

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:13.666
Hey Kevin?

00:35:13.666 --> 00:35:15.416
Yes, LeBron?

00:35:15.416 --> 00:35:16.541
I miss you.

00:35:16.541 --> 00:35:18.750
I...

00:35:18.750 --> 00:35:19.291
I miss you too

00:35:19.291 --> 00:35:20.416
All right, guys...

00:35:20.416 --> 00:35:23.416
let’s maybe keep the overt tampering to a minimum.

00:35:23.416 --> 00:35:25.166
OK, then. Who's next?

00:35:25.166 --> 00:35:25.916
House Hawks?

00:35:25.916 --> 00:35:28.375
Wait, every house here has to go? Ugh.

00:35:28.375 --> 00:35:31.666
Yes. House Hawks, please go ahead.

00:35:31.666 --> 00:35:33.125
All right

00:35:33.125 --> 00:35:37.166
Um, dear lottery gods, our house is on the rise

00:35:37.166 --> 00:35:38.291
If Zion joins us—

00:35:38.291 --> 00:35:40.375
maybe 42-year-old Vince Carter

00:35:40.375 --> 00:35:42.666
won’t have to play 17 minutes a battle

00:35:42.666 --> 00:35:44.875
OK, who else? Minnesota?

00:35:44.875 --> 00:35:46.166
I mean, how many No. 1 picks

00:35:46.166 --> 00:35:48.416
do you guys need to make the tournament?

00:35:48.416 --> 00:35:50.041
Apparently more than three

00:35:51.916 --> 00:35:52.666
This is fun

00:35:52.666 --> 00:35:53.750
Hey, do us

00:35:53.750 --> 00:35:54.166
No

00:35:54.916 --> 00:35:56.416
Who else? House Wizards?

00:35:56.416 --> 00:35:59.291
I mean, who wouldn’t want to play with Dwight Howard?

00:35:59.291 --> 00:35:59.916
By the way,

00:35:59.916 --> 00:36:02.125
when does John Wall’s supermax start?

00:36:02.125 --> 00:36:03.250
Next year?

00:36:03.250 --> 00:36:04.666
Asking for a friend

00:36:04.666 --> 00:36:06.916
OK, who else we got? House Bulls?

00:36:06.916 --> 00:36:07.791
Oh yeah, I’m sure Zion wants

00:36:07.791 --> 00:36:09.791
to spend his first year having knights-only meetings

00:36:09.791 --> 00:36:12.041
-about how many push-ups are OK.
-OK. OK. All right. LeBron...

00:36:12.041 --> 00:36:13.166
please show a little respect.

00:36:13.166 --> 00:36:14.416
For many of these houses,

00:36:14.416 --> 00:36:16.166
this is the highlight of their season.

00:36:16.166 --> 00:36:17.625
Here, here!

00:36:17.625 --> 00:36:19.916
Oh yeah, and why is that?

00:36:19.916 --> 00:36:21.750
Maybe instead of looking to the gods,

00:36:21.750 --> 00:36:23.666
you all should be looking at yourselves.

00:36:24.416 --> 00:36:27.541
Rubbish houses with uninspiring Lord Commanders,

00:36:27.541 --> 00:36:29.916
foolish masters of trade,

00:36:29.916 --> 00:36:31.041
arrogant lords

00:36:31.041 --> 00:36:31.916
You’re banned!

00:36:31.916 --> 00:36:33.166
These are things a knight,

00:36:33.166 --> 00:36:35.625
no matter how great, can't overcome.

00:36:35.625 --> 00:36:37.000
I learned that the hard way

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:40.791
Zion may be the Prince who was Promised,

00:36:40.791 --> 00:36:42.791
but he will not save you.

00:36:42.791 --> 00:36:45.666
Because if you don’t give a GOAT the support he needs,

00:36:45.666 --> 00:36:47.541
then he’s gonna walk out the door.

00:36:47.541 --> 00:36:49.875
and all you’re gonna be left with...

00:36:49.875 --> 00:36:51.666
...is poop on the floor.

00:36:51.666 --> 00:36:52.416
All right

00:36:52.416 --> 00:36:55.125
Well, on that note...

00:36:55.125 --> 00:36:58.416
why don't we go ahead and see who got the first pick?

00:36:58.416 --> 00:37:01.416
And the winner of the Zion lottery is...

00:37:01.416 --> 00:37:02.291
House Pelicans!

00:37:02.291 --> 00:37:07.750
[Murmurs of disappointment. Gayle Benson cheers ecstatically.]

00:37:23.625 --> 00:37:24.583
Your Grace?

00:37:24.958 --> 00:37:27.375
You wanted to see me?

00:37:27.375 --> 00:37:28.708
Yes

00:37:30.833 --> 00:37:34.875
I like to pretend they’re…little eggs

00:37:34.875 --> 00:37:36.458
You see, the lower houses,

00:37:36.458 --> 00:37:38.958
they are the hens.

00:37:38.958 --> 00:37:40.458
And I...

00:37:40.458 --> 00:37:43.625
am the fox that snatches their little babies.

00:37:43.625 --> 00:37:45.625
You’ve collected so many…

00:37:45.625 --> 00:37:47.875
So much talent

00:37:48.833 --> 00:37:50.833
almost, uh, too much

00:37:50.833 --> 00:37:53.833
In Bostonia, there is no such thing as too much.

00:37:53.833 --> 00:37:54.500
I know one thing

00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:56.958
Lord Pop would have never lost control of this house

00:37:56.958 --> 00:37:59.208
Pfft...Spurs of the East...

00:37:59.208 --> 00:38:00.250
Lucky for you,

00:38:00.250 --> 00:38:02.958
there’s one last road trip before the tournament starts.

00:38:02.958 --> 00:38:04.375
I suggest you find a way

00:38:04.375 --> 00:38:07.375
to get our knights on the same page.

00:38:07.375 --> 00:38:08.875
Or else…

00:38:08.875 --> 00:38:11.625
You would never. This city loves me.

00:38:11.625 --> 00:38:14.250
Like they loved The King in the Fourth?

00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:15.208
Get it done

00:38:23.833 --> 00:38:26.500
Unbelievable we gotta share a tent with the rotation guys

00:38:26.500 --> 00:38:28.000
We was the heroes last year!

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:30.250
If you’re feeling cramped, expand your mind

00:38:30.250 --> 00:38:33.000
Squires these days...so entitled

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:34.750
Better stop calling us squires, Marcus

00:38:34.750 --> 00:38:36.833
You don’t scare me, Terry

00:38:36.833 --> 00:38:38.250
You think you’re some wise veteran—

00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:41.500
What is that?

00:38:41.500 --> 00:38:45.250
I’ve seen that before. That there is a Soul Box.

00:38:45.250 --> 00:38:47.500
When you sign with House Spurs,

00:38:47.500 --> 00:38:51.083
your soul and personality go into that box.

00:38:51.083 --> 00:38:54.000
So it’s like a…Spurs culture thing?

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:55.625
I didn’t want it to come to this

00:38:55.625 --> 00:38:57.625
but there is too much talent here in this room

00:38:57.625 --> 00:39:00.000
for us to be treading water in the fourth seed.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:03.833
The Soul Box will help us contain our emotions and our egos,

00:39:03.833 --> 00:39:06.000
so that this group can reach its potential.

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.250
Also makes you dull as dirt

00:39:08.250 --> 00:39:12.000
That thing's the reason nobody heard of me in San Antonio

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:13.750
Oh, yeah. That’s the reason.

00:39:13.750 --> 00:39:15.250
I’ll do it

00:39:15.833 --> 00:39:17.000
All right, Al

00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:19.500
I want you to close your eyes and place your hand on the box

00:39:20.708 --> 00:39:22.333
Ser Al Horford,

00:39:22.333 --> 00:39:23.875
do you hereby commit fully,

00:39:23.875 --> 00:39:28.125
to sacrifice your soul for the good of House Celtics?

00:39:28.750 --> 00:39:29.625
Aye

00:39:35.125 --> 00:39:36.250
So did it work or what?

00:39:38.375 --> 00:39:39.750
He didn’t flinch!

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:43.500
All right, who’s next? Anyone?

00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:45.375
I’ll do it

00:39:45.375 --> 00:39:46.125
OK, no. Lucky—

00:39:46.125 --> 00:39:48.125
Gimme that box. I’ll do it.

00:39:48.125 --> 00:39:50.125
-Put my soul right in that box
-Thanks, Lucky, but this is for knights

00:39:51.125 --> 00:39:52.500
Marcus the Smart?

00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:57.333
I…I can’t. I’m sorry. My whole game is about emotion.

00:39:58.083 --> 00:39:58.750
Jaylen?

00:39:58.750 --> 00:40:01.458
Uh, I’m just worried about my brand is all

00:40:01.458 --> 00:40:02.875
What about you, Kyrie?

00:40:02.875 --> 00:40:07.000
Ha, subjugate the light of my soul to your rectangular prism?

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:08.625
No way...

00:40:08.625 --> 00:40:10.000
I can’t even commit to next year

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.375
Wow...what a leader

00:40:11.375 --> 00:40:13.000
OK, then why don’t you do it?

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:13.833
Well, I just...

00:40:13.833 --> 00:40:16.500
don’t want to jeopardize my Mamba Mentality is all.

00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:19.000
Yeah, gods forbid you stop shooting 20-footers

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:19.375
Yeah, gods forbid you stop shooting 20-footers

00:40:19.375 --> 00:40:20.125
Oh, please. You’re one to talk.

00:40:20.125 --> 00:40:22.083
-Oh, I’m Jayson Tatum. I’m the man.
-Very funny.

00:40:22.083 --> 00:40:23.750
I’m going to House Pelicans to be the man!

00:40:23.750 --> 00:40:25.375
All right, guys. Come on!

00:40:25.375 --> 00:40:28.708
You know what? Clearly, this was a bad idea, OK?

00:40:28.708 --> 00:40:31.875
You guys are obviously not the Spurs,

00:40:31.875 --> 00:40:34.750
and I am clearly...not Lord Pop.

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:37.375
No...you’re not

00:40:41.250 --> 00:40:43.125
You’re Brad Stevens.

00:40:43.125 --> 00:40:45.625
The best X’s and O’s man I’ve ever known

00:40:45.625 --> 00:40:48.833
Yeah, nobody can write out-of-timeout plays like you

00:40:48.833 --> 00:40:50.375
Yeah, well, unfortunately,

00:40:50.375 --> 00:40:53.500
there’s no timeout long enough for me to fix all of THIS team’s issues.

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:56.833
But what if there was

00:40:56.833 --> 00:40:57.750
Who said that?

00:40:59.125 --> 00:41:00.125
The Time Lord…

00:41:00.125 --> 00:41:02.375
Wait, ‘Time Lord'? I thought that was just a nickname.

00:41:02.375 --> 00:41:04.875
There’s a lot of things people don’t know about me

00:41:04.875 --> 00:41:05.833
Don’t get enough minutes

00:41:05.833 --> 00:41:07.083
Tell me about it

00:41:07.083 --> 00:41:11.125
But I’m pretty versatile. I can rebound, I can block,

00:41:11.125 --> 00:41:12.208
and I can stop time.

00:41:12.208 --> 00:41:14.000
Where’d you learn how to do that?

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:15.458
Texas A&amp;M

00:41:15.458 --> 00:41:17.208
But you were only there for two years!

00:41:17.208 --> 00:41:18.750
...or was I?

00:41:18.750 --> 00:41:20.708
Whoa

00:41:20.708 --> 00:41:23.458
So how does one just...stop time?

00:41:23.458 --> 00:41:24.750
Just asking questions here

00:41:24.750 --> 00:41:28.125
It's a magic potion…called So’Da

00:41:29.125 --> 00:41:32.125
Banned in the realm since Jason Kidd used it against House Lakers,

00:41:32.125 --> 00:41:34.625
late in a battle when he had no timeouts left.

00:41:34.625 --> 00:41:37.250
Exactly how long are we talking about here?

00:41:37.250 --> 00:41:38.500
It will last till either you've

00:41:38.500 --> 00:41:40.625
come up with a way to solve our problems…

00:41:40.625 --> 00:41:42.750
or 34 years...whichever comes first

00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:44.583
Why 34?

00:41:44.583 --> 00:41:46.083
It’s the Truth…

00:41:46.083 --> 00:41:47.750
34 is the Truth’s number

00:41:47.750 --> 00:41:49.625
The guy who’s worse than Dwyane Wade!

00:41:49.625 --> 00:41:52.000
Actually, no. That’s just how much So'Da I have.

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:53.708
All right, you’ve got this, Lord Commander!

00:41:53.708 --> 00:41:54.583
Yeah!

00:41:54.583 --> 00:41:57.083
-You’re Brad Stevens!
-You’re a freaking genius!
-You're smartest in the realm!

00:41:57.083 --> 00:41:58.250
We know you can do this, Lord Commander!

00:41:58.250 --> 00:41:59.583
Are you all mad?

00:41:59.583 --> 00:42:02.583
Do you really think he can just come up with some

00:42:02.583 --> 00:42:06.250
magical out-of-timeout play that’s gonna fix all of our chemistry issues?

00:42:06.250 --> 00:42:08.750
Yeah, you know what? I do.

00:42:09.750 --> 00:42:12.333
Because I’m Brad F--king Stevens

00:42:15.250 --> 00:42:17.125
Time Lord, ready when you are

00:42:17.125 --> 00:42:19.125
All right

00:42:19.125 --> 00:42:21.250
Time...

00:42:21.250 --> 00:42:21.708
OUT

00:42:21.708 --> 00:42:22.375
OH  F--K

00:42:23.375 --> 00:42:25.208
Lord Commander?

00:42:25.208 --> 00:42:26.125
You look like you’ve aged—

00:42:26.125 --> 00:42:28.000
34 years. Yep.

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:29.875
So you...you didn’t...?

00:42:29.875 --> 00:42:31.125
Nope

00:42:31.125 --> 00:42:33.000
So, what’s all that?

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:36.583
Mostly just gibberish. I gave up 20 ago, actually.

00:42:37.083 --> 00:42:38.083
What’s THAT?

00:42:40.375 --> 00:42:42.125
All right,

00:42:42.125 --> 00:42:46.750
I’ve got some good news and some bad news.

00:42:46.750 --> 00:42:49.125
Bad news first

00:42:49.125 --> 00:42:52.458
Lucky got frozen in time with me

00:42:54.375 --> 00:42:55.833
The So'Da spilled on him

00:42:55.833 --> 00:42:57.875
Oh, no. What have I—

00:42:57.875 --> 00:42:59.208
Unfortunately for Lucky,

00:42:59.208 --> 00:43:02.958
he swore a blood oath to always perform during timeouts,

00:43:02.958 --> 00:43:06.708
obviously never thinking he’d, well...yeah.

00:43:08.083 --> 00:43:11.875
But he kept performing. He was juggling. Dancing.

00:43:11.875 --> 00:43:13.958
Doing those wacky dunks

00:43:13.958 --> 00:43:16.750
Man, was he funny

00:43:16.750 --> 00:43:20.875
By year two, he was mostly performing stuff that could be done from a chair,

00:43:20.875 --> 00:43:25.625
like balancing bowls, singing, whatever.

00:43:25.625 --> 00:43:29.083
It was around year three where...he stopped talking

00:43:29.875 --> 00:43:34.875
He was just miming and deliriously flailing his arms

00:43:34.958 --> 00:43:37.708
By year four, I thought he was doing this long bit

00:43:37.708 --> 00:43:39.458
where he would just play dead.

00:43:39.458 --> 00:43:42.708
By year five, I realized...

00:43:43.333 --> 00:43:44.708
it wasn't a bit.

00:43:47.875 --> 00:43:49.833
So, um...

00:43:49.833 --> 00:43:51.125
what’s the good news?

00:43:51.125 --> 00:43:54.125
Well, I came up with a few pretty clever inbound plays

00:43:54.125 --> 00:43:55.750
that might get us to the second round.

00:44:08.875 --> 00:44:11.875
And together, we'll rule the world...

00:44:11.875 --> 00:44:13.666
from edge to edge.

00:44:13.750 --> 00:44:16.375
Thank you, Kyrie. I’ll be in touch.

00:44:21.625 --> 00:44:23.500
What’s ​he​ doing here?

00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:25.125
Oh, he was just...

00:44:25.125 --> 00:44:26.916
asking questions.

00:44:27.166 --> 00:44:28.750
What are ​you​ doing here?

00:44:28.750 --> 00:44:30.000
I thought it was quite generous we

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:31.791
let you hang around for six battles.

00:44:31.791 --> 00:44:34.000
Now you’re just being greedy with my time.

00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:37.416
Clearly my defense has yet to earn your respect.

00:44:37.416 --> 00:44:40.666
I respect your​ effort​...

00:44:40.666 --> 00:44:44.125
and I heard you said nice things about me after the battle.

00:44:44.125 --> 00:44:45.875
You’re a worthy opponent.

00:44:45.875 --> 00:44:48.250
If you like me as your opponent,

00:44:48.250 --> 00:44:50.166
you’d love me as your teammate.

00:44:50.166 --> 00:44:53.166
Free-agent talk will wait until​ after ​the tournament.

00:44:53.541 --> 00:44:56.541
Oh, come on. Have a little fun...

00:44:56.541 --> 00:44:59.000
gods know you’re not having any here.

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:02.375
If you want some scrub, go to an eliminated house.

00:45:02.375 --> 00:45:04.625
If you want a king...

00:45:04.625 --> 00:45:05.666
earn him.

00:45:08.625 --> 00:45:12.250
Wow, pure gold.

00:45:12.250 --> 00:45:15.000
It's funny. I thought your throne would be made of salt.

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:18.500
You’re insolent. I’ve dropped 40 on men for less.

00:45:18.500 --> 00:45:20.250
They were lesser men.

00:45:20.250 --> 00:45:22.875
Oh, please. Didn’t I just drop 50 on you?

00:45:22.875 --> 00:45:25.375
We’re done here.

00:45:25.375 --> 00:45:26.916
Well then,

00:45:26.916 --> 00:45:29.916
I guess good luck in New York.

00:45:29.916 --> 00:45:32.125
Who says I'm going to New York?

00:45:32.125 --> 00:45:35.125
Oh...everybody.

00:45:35.916 --> 00:45:39.250
The Garden is the biggest stage in the Realm.

00:45:39.250 --> 00:45:42.250
I would be the GOAT if I turned that house around.

00:45:42.250 --> 00:45:44.666
And if you fail...on this

00:45:44.666 --> 00:45:47.041
“biggest stage in the Realm"?

00:45:47.416 --> 00:45:49.375
Wah! Can’t win with those cats.

00:45:49.375 --> 00:45:53.125
Listen to your burner. You can’t win with those cats.

00:45:53.125 --> 00:45:55.625
What you need is a dog.

00:45:55.625 --> 00:45:59.666
A hungry, loyal hound.

00:45:59.666 --> 00:46:02.750
You're proud to be a dog, eh? That’s a new one.

00:46:02.750 --> 00:46:04.250
Men love dogs.

00:46:04.250 --> 00:46:07.500
What they loathe are snakes.

00:46:07.500 --> 00:46:10.500
If you’re trying to lure me to House Clippers,

00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:12.416
you’re doing an awful job.

00:46:12.416 --> 00:46:14.375
You know, now that I think about it,

00:46:14.375 --> 00:46:16.500
House Clippers would be a terrible fit.

00:46:16.500 --> 00:46:19.750
I mean, we all know you only take...

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:21.416
the hardest road.

00:46:21.416 --> 00:46:25.041
And House Clippers would be…smooth sailing, really.

00:46:25.041 --> 00:46:28.041
You’ve got Lord West, builder of empires,

00:46:28.041 --> 00:46:32.541
two max slots, the best lord commander in the Realm

00:46:32.541 --> 00:46:39.875
and a bunch of hungry, loyal dogs just looking for their alpha.

00:46:39.916 --> 00:46:42.250
It’s almost too easy.

00:46:42.250 --> 00:46:44.125
And besides,

00:46:44.125 --> 00:46:46.666
if you came to Los Angeles,

00:46:46.666 --> 00:46:50.375
It would be so unfair to King James.

00:46:50.375 --> 00:46:54.625
Upstaged night after night in his own city,

00:46:54.625 --> 00:46:58.500
by the man who was always second-best.

00:46:58.500 --> 00:47:02.916
You know, for a free agent, you’re very loyal to House Clippers.

00:47:02.916 --> 00:47:05.125
Loyalty is what dogs do best.

00:47:05.541 --> 00:47:07.500
Hey, uh, KD?

00:47:07.500 --> 00:47:09.750
It’s my turn to sit on the throne.

00:47:10.375 --> 00:47:11.291
I should be going.

00:47:11.291 --> 00:47:13.875
You’ve been very generous with your time.

00:47:14.625 --> 00:47:15.500
We should talk.

00:47:22.041 --> 00:47:23.375
Well, maybe if you didn't miss all those threes...

00:47:23.375 --> 00:47:25.166
We got jinxed by The Truth...

00:47:25.166 --> 00:47:26.000
He's a bloody monster!

00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:27.791
Who could've expected Fred VanVleet?

00:47:27.791 --> 00:47:30.291
Men, we gather today to celebrate

00:47:30.291 --> 00:47:32.375
For if the whispers are true,

00:47:32.375 --> 00:47:35.375
Ser Giannis will be anointed the Most Valuable Knight.

00:47:37.625 --> 00:47:40.625
Thank you, but how can I be deemed the ‘most valuable’

00:47:40.625 --> 00:47:43.625
when I couldn’t even get us to the Finals?

00:47:43.625 --> 00:47:46.625
King James used to crush House Raptors without breaking a sweat.

00:47:47.291 --> 00:47:51.875
They were a different house then. They didn’t have that...monster.

00:47:51.875 --> 00:47:55.541
We should be proud. We won 60 battles this year.

00:47:55.541 --> 00:47:57.750
Yes, but it is all for nothing.

00:47:57.750 --> 00:48:01.291
Our tournament is over. The offseason has come.

00:48:02.500 --> 00:48:05.500
If the Maesters are right, Durant will be heading East,

00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:09.666
which means it’s going to be hard for us to even make conference finals again.

00:48:09.666 --> 00:48:12.666
We should ride home. We should test the market.

00:48:13.791 --> 00:48:18.291
Maybe sign with House Pelicans again? Or House Bulls?

00:48:18.291 --> 00:48:20.500
I hear House Lakers needs talent.

00:48:21.500 --> 00:48:24.000
As a former knight of House Suns,

00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:27.000
I know misery, and this is not it.

00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:31.541
Sure, we're defeated, but we are not without hope,

00:48:31.541 --> 00:48:37.000
for we have the honor of fighting alongside true greatness.

00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:40.000
Not just of skill, but of character.

00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:43.000
The King of the North may rule the East for now,

00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:46.750
but I recognize only one true king.

00:48:46.750 --> 00:48:50.125
And his name is long and full of letters.

00:48:50.125 --> 00:48:57.375
Giannis Antetokounmpo is my king from this day until his last day.

00:48:57.375 --> 00:49:00.375
And you know what? I DO want to be here.​

00:49:01.416 --> 00:49:05.666
Last year, I fought side by side with King James.

00:49:05.666 --> 00:49:09.291
I didn’t think we’d find another GOAT in the East...

00:49:09.291 --> 00:49:11.291
not in my career.

00:49:11.291 --> 00:49:13.541
But I was wrong!

00:49:13.541 --> 00:49:19.666
Giannis is not only the Most Valuable Knight in the Realm. He is

00:49:19.666 --> 00:49:22.250
The King in the East!

00:49:22.250 --> 00:49:24.041
Assuming Kawhi leaves, of course!

00:49:24.041 --> 00:49:28.125
I remember the days when Brandon Knight was our​ best ​knight...

00:49:28.125 --> 00:49:30.041
or maybe it was Ramon Sessions.

00:49:30.041 --> 00:49:36.375
As Giannis has grown, so has the dignity and respect of this house.

00:49:36.375 --> 00:49:38.500
We have not known hope like this

00:49:38.500 --> 00:49:42.125
since the days of Ser Alcindor and the Big O...

00:49:42.125 --> 00:49:45.125
and it’s all thanks to Giannis.

00:49:45.125 --> 00:49:48.125
The King in the East!

00:49:48.375 --> 00:49:49.750
To next year!

00:49:49.750 --> 00:49:52.500
-The King in the East!
-To next season!

00:49:52.500 --> 00:49:53.625
-The King in the East!
-To the future!

00:49:53.625 --> 00:50:03.166
-The King in the East!
-The King in the East!
-The King in the East!

00:50:04.875 --> 00:50:07.875
Oh, how quickly they forget

00:50:07.875 --> 00:50:10.416
Nine years, I ruled the East.

00:50:10.416 --> 00:50:14.875
From 3-1 down, I slayed the Warriors

00:50:14.875 --> 00:50:19.000
From the brink of baldness, I have restored my hairline

00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:22.750
And from the ashes of a lost season...

00:50:22.750 --> 00:50:24.791
I will return.

00:50:24.791 --> 00:50:25.916
Rested

00:50:25.916 --> 00:50:27.291
Reborn

00:50:27.291 --> 00:50:28.875
Re-groined

00:50:28.875 --> 00:50:30.750
To reclaim my throne

00:50:30.750 --> 00:50:33.291
As the true king...

00:50:33.291 --> 00:50:35.791
Of...the...

00:50:35.791 --> 00:50:53.375
Sea!

00:50:53.375 --> 00:50:54.291
Jam!

00:50:54.291 --> 00:50:56.375
All right. Cut, cut!

00:50:56.375 --> 00:50:58.791
JaVale, you dunked on the wrong basket

00:50:58.791 --> 00:51:00.791
And Melo, what are you doing in front of me?

00:51:00.791 --> 00:51:02.000
Why aren't you in the banana canoe?

00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:03.916
Because I'm a star, Lebron

00:51:03.916 --> 00:51:05.500
And stars should be in leading roles

00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:06.375
All right, well, hold on—

00:51:06.375 --> 00:51:09.250
Matt Barnacle, stop strangling Derek with the fishing wire

00:51:09.250 --> 00:51:12.250
Well, it says here in the script that I swam 95 miles to kick his ass

00:51:12.250 --> 00:51:14.500
so I figured I'd—figured I'd do it.

00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:15.625
Completely uncalled for!

00:51:15.625 --> 00:51:17.500
You'll never be Kobe, LeBron!

00:51:17.500 --> 00:51:19.916
-Yeah, you ain't never gonna win an Oscar!
-Yeah!

00:51:19.916 --> 00:51:22.166
OK, can someone get those guys out of here?

00:51:22.166 --> 00:51:24.791
Also, where did Magic go? He was supposed to be here.

00:51:24.791 --> 00:51:25.541
Um, excuse me?

00:51:25.541 --> 00:51:28.000
Can I play Kevin of Durant in the Monstarfish?

00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:31.000
No, Brandon. You're—you're in the wave.

00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:32.500
Ugh, I think we need to do a rewrite.

00:51:32.500 --> 00:51:34.166
This is just not working.

00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:35.916
I stand by it

00:51:35.916 --> 00:51:39.250
I'd take Mike Muscala over Brook Lopez a hundred times out of a hundred

00:51:39.583 --> 00:51:40.416
[sigh]

00:51:40.666 --> 00:51:41.666
You know, Larry?

00:51:41.791 --> 00:51:43.958
I'm really glad I quit House Lakers

00:51:43.958 --> 00:51:46.791
Now I can just watch battles and send ravens,

00:51:46.791 --> 00:51:49.458
hang out with you, my best, rival-friend,

00:51:49.458 --> 00:51:51.166
and none of it's tampering!

00:51:51.166 --> 00:51:53.625
Ugh, I just wish there was a way to know when a new Game of Zones came out

00:51:53.625 --> 00:51:55.166
Subscribe! Subscribe!

00:51:55.166 --> 00:51:56.708
Come on, Larry. Use your person voice

00:51:57.541 --> 00:51:59.208
What I was saying, you idiot–

00:51:59.208 --> 00:52:01.041
Ah, bup! No trash talk, Larry Bird

00:52:01.041 --> 00:52:01.750
We're past that 

00:52:02.916 --> 00:52:05.000
If you just hit the "subscribe" button...

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:07.708
they will notify you when a new Game of Zones comes out

